# ClearLine — project rules

ClearLine is a field console for VoIP technicians. Users are standing in a
wiring closet, on a phone, mid-cutover, often one-handed. Every decision
below follows from that.

## The design language is called Instrument

Not "dark mode." The reference is test equipment — a signal analyzer, a
spectrum monitor. Dark because the room is dark. Glowing because light
means live. One accent because a second accent would imply a second signal.

**The rule that settles most arguments:**

> If a visual property does not encode state, remove it.

- Colour encodes severity
- Glow encodes activity
- Opacity encodes relevance
- Motion encodes real progress

A border that is only a border is decoration. Cut it.

## Tokens

Never introduce a new colour. Every value comes from `src/styles.css`:

`--bg0` `--bg1` `--bg2` `--glass` `--rim` `--ink` `--ink-soft` `--muted`
`--line` `--line-strong` `--cta` `--cta-soft` `--accent` `--accent-soft`
`--ok` `--warn` `--err` `--radius` `--radius-sm` `--font` `--display` `--mono`

Semantic colours (`--ok` / `--warn` / `--err`) are allowed anywhere because
they encode state. That is the rule working, not an exception to it.

Both `[data-theme='dark']` and light must work. Tokens are theme-scoped
already, so using them correctly gets this for free.

## Motion

Import from `src/lib/motion.js`. Three curves, product-wide:

- `SPRING` — arrivals, landings, snaps
- `SETTLE` — fills, growth, reveals
- `SNAP` — hover, focus, colour changes

A fourth curve is a bug. A hand-written `cubic-bezier` in a component is a
bug. `prefersReducedMotion` is imported, never redefined.

Reduced motion means **skip to the end state**, never half-play.

## Copy — the disclosure ladder

Every string sits on exactly one rung:

| Rung | Form | Limit |
|---|---|---|
| Eyebrow | uppercase, `.18em` tracking | 3–6 words |
| Lede | one sentence, sentence case | ≤ 12 words |
| Why | paragraph behind a `<details>` toggle | any |
| Reference | table, drawer, linked doc | any |

**No paragraph renders by default.** If a string exceeds 12 words it becomes
a why-drawer, becomes structure, or gets cut. Rationale never occupies
primary space.

When prose is actually data — timings, offsets, severities, checklists —
promote it to structure rather than hiding it. A timeline rail beats a
sentence explaining offsets.

Sentence case everywhere. No exclamation marks. No "please", "simply",
"successfully". Errors say what happened and what to do, in one sentence.

## Diagrams

Applies to `CallFlowDiagram.jsx` and `TopologyEditor.jsx`:

- Edges are **conduits** — a dim track plus a travelling lit segment
  (`stroke-dasharray: .1 .9`, animated `stroke-dashoffset`). No arrowheads.
- Nodes are **terminals** — dark fill, 1px rim, no shadow. Accent glow only
  on the live path.
- Hierarchy is **luminance**. Off-path drops to ~22% opacity. Dimmed, never
  greyed, never desaturated.
- Background is a **dot field**, not grid lines.
- On mount, nodes stagger in **following the direction of flow**.
- Navigation is a **path rail** (horizontal chip strip), not a minimap.
  Users have a linear question — where does this call end up.

## Quality floor — non-negotiable

- Visible `:focus-visible` outline on every interactive element
- Keyboard reachable; arrow-key nav on anything with a spatial arrangement
- `aria-label` on icon-only buttons, `role="status"` on live regions
- Works at 360px wide
- No new dependencies without asking

## Things that are already correct — do not restyle

- `FluidDock.jsx` — the parametric dock path and shoulder/socket maths
- `AuthGooeyHero` in `AuthScreens.jsx` — the metaball filter
- The token block at the top of `styles.css`
- `.app-atmosphere` — the ambient bloom

## Working style

One task per commit. Do not refactor adjacent code opportunistically. If a
task touches more than three files, stop and say so before starting.
